39
00:02:53,399 --> 00:02:55,726
remote origin already exists.:

40
00:02:55,726 --> 00:02:57,821
a clone already has origin.

41
00:02:57,821 --> 00:03:00,691
The snippet assumes a fresh git init.

42
00:03:00,691 --> 00:03:04,338
Check what origin currently is before deciding:

43
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:10,908
If the URL is what you wanted, there is nothing to do.

44
00:03:10,908 --> 00:03:15,804
If not, change it (set-url), never add a second origin:

45
00:03:17,567 --> 00:03:18,280
